 "text": "You know that moment when those new headlights come at you and everything goes white? You squint at the line on the road and just hope you're still in your lane. And if you wear glasses, it's even worse. These are night driving glasses that go right over your regular ones. The yellow lens is polarized, so it cuts the glare from oncoming headlights. And look, there's a little yellow window on each side, so the glare can't sneak in from the side. Honestly, why did nobody tell us about these sooner? Girls, the clocks go back November first, so it's dark on the drive home. Keep a pair in your car and grab one for your mom. It's in the orange cart.",
